-- title:
--   Freeness of the minimal-level Hecke module over its operator algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual Galois representation over $k$ (a $k$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ factoring through a finite level) which is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\overline{k}$ is irreducible. Let $S,S_{\min}$ be finite sets of naturals with every element of $S$ prime, $p\in S_{\min}\subseteq S$, such that for primes $q\neq p$ one has $q\in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\rho$ fails to be unramified at $q$ (some $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of some valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ acts nontrivially), and such that for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, the adic representation associated with $\rho$ is unipotent on inertia at $q$: every inertia element at every place over $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$. Let $N\neq 0$ be squarefree, with every prime divisor of $N$ in $S$, every prime of $S_{\min}$ other than $p$ dividing $N$, and every prime divisor $q\neq p$ of $N$ lying in $S_{\min}$; assume moreover that if $p\mid N$ then the adic representation associated with $\rho$ is not flat at $p$. Let $r$ be any natural number. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic weight-two Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the Hecke operators away from $S$) to $k$ such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $P$, and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Finally let $\mathrm{hc}_0$ witness `BaseOpComm N r S 𝒪`, namely that the operators $\mathrm{baseOp}\,N\,r\,S\,\mathcal O\,g$ on $H^1(N,\top;\mathcal O)$ commute pairwise as $g$ ranges over the generator index set $\mathrm{Gen}\,N\,r\,S$. The conclusion concerns the module $M=$ [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.baseML N r S 𝒪 θ hc₀`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModuleBase.html#L31), the module `ML` of the Hecke data with generators $\mathrm{Gen}\,N\,r\,S$, operators $\mathrm{baseOp}$ and residual eigensystem $g\mapsto\theta(T_g)$; its free algebra is the polynomial ring $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Gen}\,N\,r\,S)\,\mathcal O$. The assertion is that $M$ is free as a module over the image in $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}M$ of that polynomial algebra acting by scalar multiplication, i.e. over the subalgebra of $\mathcal O$-endomorphisms of $M$ generated by the given Hecke operators.
--
--   This is the multiplicity-one statement at the minimal level in its cohomological form: the localised first cohomology module of $\Gamma_0(N)$ with $\mathcal O$-coefficients, taken at the non-Eisenstein maximal ideal attached to $\bar\rho$, is free over the algebra of endomorphisms generated by the Hecke operators $T_\ell$ for $\ell\nmid N$ outside $S$ (and the auxiliary parameter $r$). It is used by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_moduleFree_linearEquiv_auxLevel_baseML`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_moduleFree_linearEquiv_auxLevel_baseML) to produce the free module over the local anemic Hecke algebra of cusp forms that serves as the minimal-level input of the Taylor–Wiles patching argument.
